{
  "dom_id": "step-q101922",
  "name": "Question 7",
  "problem": "If $x,y,$ and $z$ are elements of $B$, but $v$ and $w$ are not, then which of the following is true?",
  "worked_solution": "If $a$ is an element of $S,$ we write $a\\in S.$ Otherwise, if $a$ is *not* an element of $S,$ we write $a\\notin S.$\n\n- Since $x,y,$ and $z$ are elements of $B,$ we write $x,y,z\\in B.$\n\n- Since $v$ and $w$ are *not* elements of $B,$ we write $v,w\\notin B.$\n\nAll together, we have the following statement:\n\n$\\,$  $x,y,z\\in B$ and $v,w\\notin B$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
